[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)(4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m First, let's simplify the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)(4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)),
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m and
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Combining these, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Separating the real and imaginary parts, we get:
