[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Simplifying the real part, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m We need to maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\), so the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Let's calculate this value using Python.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m b = -432
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m # Maximum value of a*cos(theta) + b*sin(theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m max_value = math.sqrt(a**2 + b**2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m print(max_value)
