[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form: \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta} = (24 - 36i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta - i(24\sin\theta - 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Adding these two expressions together, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta - i(24\sin\theta - 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Combining the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + (4 \cdot 75\sin\theta + 4 \cdot 117\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta)i
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta) + i(276\sin\theta + 504\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). To maximize this real part, we need to maximize the expression \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). This can be done by expressing it in the form \(R\cos(\theta + \phi)\), where \(R = \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m R = \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 360\sqrt{3}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The maximum value of \(R\cos(\theta + \phi)\) is \(R\), which is \(360\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
