[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Simplifying the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta + 75i \sin \theta + 117i \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) = 4((75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + i(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta)),
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m and
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)} \cdot \frac{\cos \theta - i \sin \theta}{\cos \theta - i \sin \theta} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)}{4(\cos^2 \theta + \sin^2 \theta)} = \frac{96 \cos \theta + 144 \sin \theta + i(144 \cos \theta - 96 \sin \theta)}{4} = 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i(36 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4((75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + i(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta)) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i(36 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta) = (300 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta) + i(300 \sin \theta + 468 \cos \theta + 36 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta) = (324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta) + i(336 \cos \theta + 276 \sin \theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
