[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Substituting \(z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + 36i(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = 24\cos\theta + 24i\sin\theta + 36i\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = (24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + (24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta) = (4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + 24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The real part of the expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m We need to maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). We can use the identity \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta = R\cos(\theta + \phi)\) where \(R = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\) and \(\tan\phi = \frac{b}{a}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 432\), so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Thus, the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\) is \(540\). Therefore, the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
