[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The real part of the expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of the expression. The expression \(324 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta\) can be written as \(R \cos(\theta + \phi)\) where \(R = \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2}\).
