[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to find the largest possible real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Substituting \(z = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta + 75i \sin \theta + 117i \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) = 4((75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + i (75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{\cos \theta + i \sin \theta} = (24 + 36i) \cdot (\cos \theta - i \sin \theta) = 24 \cos \theta + 24i \sin \theta - 36i \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = (24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta) + i (24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m Adding these two results, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 4((75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + i (75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta)) + (24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta) + i (24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m = (4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta) + i (4(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta) + 24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m = (300 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta) + i (300 \sin \theta + 468 \cos \theta + 24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m = (324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta) + i (324 \sin \theta + 432 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of the sinusoidal function. The expression \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) can be written as \(R \cos(\theta + \phi)\) where \(R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3001510)[0m So the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) is \(540\). Therefore, the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
